{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves","id":1197775,"title":"Skirting Around the Werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-20T16:15:42-07:00","id":1197775,"title":"Skirting Around the Werewolves","content":"Alright, so I'm running a Mage game that will soon be adding a couple of Uktena, Nuwisha and (very confused, time displaced) Camazotz NPC's to complicate the cabal's mission. <br /> <br /> Here's the issue: anyone who bothers keeping track of the opinions of forum posters knows that my opinion on WtA itself is icy on a good day, and a lot of that comes from the fact that I think it's themes are flawed on a fundamental level. But I want to have shapechangers in my game. How do I integrate Fera and other assorted WtA ephemera into my game without dragging in all the attendant baggage and accidentally establishing the Gaian worldview as the &quot;one true reality&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T16:22:01-07:00","id":1197776,"title":"","content":"By just not mentioning the \u2018big picture\u2019 of the Triat and Gaia? Have them just be there on personal interests and local issues. Added effect of leaving some wriggle room for setting changes in the future, should you wish to re-incorporate the rest of the setting (in the way of \u201cthey didn\u2019t bother to mention it back then, since you were all outsiders\u201d). It works for crossovers in the CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:21:02-07:00","id":1197790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves#post1197775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so I'm running a Mage game that will soon be adding a couple of Uktena, Nuwisha and (very confused, time displaced) Camazotz NPC's to complicate the cabal's mission. <br /> <br /> Here's the issue: anyone who bothers keeping track of the opinions of forum posters knows that my opinion on WtA itself is icy on a good day, and a lot of that comes from the fact that I think it's themes are flawed on a fundamental level. But I want to have shapechangers in my game. How do I integrate Fera and other assorted WtA ephemera into my game without dragging in all the attendant baggage and accidentally establishing the Gaian worldview as the &amp;quot;one true reality&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give us some more details about what you don't like about W:tA, that may give us a better idea of how to incorporate them without bringing in things you don't like.<br /> <br /> In fact, to expand in that, what do you like about W:tA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:26:17-07:00","id":1197794,"title":"","content":"Do you have Fera pcs or npcs? If they are PCs why did you let people play them if you generally don't like them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:38:02-07:00","id":1197798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves?p=1197790#post1197790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you give us some more details about what you don't like about W:tA, that may give us a better idea of how to incorporate them without bringing in things you don't like.<br /> <br /> In fact, to expand in that, what do you like about W:tA?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I suppose it was a little bit pompous of me to assume that people were already familiar with my opinions. I just wanted to avoid being &quot;that guy&quot; on the forums that constantly trumpets one opinion very loudly and frequently, y'know?<br /> <br /> Basically, I think the whole shtick with the Triat is kind of problematically reductive. I <i>especially </i>don't like the way that the Weaver is said to pervade all aspects of technology and civilization, reinforcing the obnoxious &quot;science/technology = rigid conformity&quot; theme that Mage has spent 4 editions trying to get away from. There's also the fact that the Gaia aligned factions seem to operate on a principle of theological voluntarism that is presented as the absolute, in-canon right answer. <br /> <br /> That said, the individual Tribes and Breeds do have some compelling stuff in them. Their histories and conflicts are pretty interesting and they certainly have some neat powers and abilities to showcase when it comes time for a gonzo action scene. For better or worse, I also kinda' enjoy a lot of the Wyrm's trappings, particularly Pentex, which is such a cartoonishly nonsensical caricature it comes off as almost endearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T17:39:01-07:00","id":1197801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves?p=1197794#post1197794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have Fera pcs or npcs? If they are PCs why did you let people play them if you generally don't like them?</div> </div> </div> </div>NPCs. The PC's are an Ecstatic, a Hermetic and an Akashic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T18:05:23-07:00","id":1197814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves?p=1197798#post1197798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. I suppose it was a little bit pompous of me to assume that people were already familiar with my opinions. I just wanted to avoid being &amp;quot;that guy&amp;quot; on the forums that constantly trumpets one opinion very loudly and frequently, y'know?<br /> <br /> Basically, I think the whole shtick with the Triat is kind of problematically reductive. I <i>especially </i>don't like the way that the Weaver is said to pervade all aspects of technology and civilization, reinforcing the obnoxious &amp;quot;science/technology = rigid conformity&amp;quot; theme that Mage has spent 4 editions trying to get away from. There's also the fact that the Gaia aligned factions seem to operate on a principle of theological voluntarism that is presented as the absolute, in-canon right answer. <br /> <br /> That said, the individual Tribes and Breeds do have some compelling stuff in them. Their histories and conflicts are pretty interesting and they certainly have some neat powers and abilities to showcase when it comes time for a gonzo action scene. For better or worse, I also kinda' enjoy a lot of the Wyrm's trappings, particularly Pentex, which is such a cartoonishly nonsensical caricature it comes off as almost endearing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since you don't like some of the cosmology and the Garou aren't the PC's then just let the Garou be wrong. One problem that I see way too often in fastastic setting is that people (or creatures) who have some sort of belief system about how everything works turn out to almost always be right. In real life, people are wrong about how the world works all the time. You can have your werewolves have certain viewpoints about Gaia and the Triat that aren't accurate. They are rags filled religious fanatics after all, it's not as though they objectively access all of the evidence.<br /> <br /> Make the truth what ever you like, the Garou culture doesn't have to know it.<br /> <br /> Or, just change what the Garou believe. It's not like you're playing W:tA and owe some allegiance to the purity of that setting. In fact, even if you were playing W:tA you could still change not only the cosmology but the also culture and religion. <br /> <br /> Feel free to change as much about W:tA as you like. It might actually make things more interesting for your players who would now be as ignorant of werewolves as their characters should be. I actually think that is a good idea to change the supporting game when ever there is a crossover, otherwise the players' OOC knowledge will affect their feelings and actions regardless of how hard you try to avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T20:39:32-07:00","id":1197865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves?p=1197798#post1197798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. I suppose it was a little bit pompous of me to assume that people were already familiar with my opinions. I just wanted to avoid being &quot;that guy&quot; on the forums that constantly trumpets one opinion very loudly and frequently, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically, I think the whole shtick with the Triat is kind of problematically reductive. I <i>especially </i>don't like the way that the Weaver is said to pervade all aspects of technology and civilization, reinforcing the obnoxious &quot;science/technology = rigid conformity&quot; theme that Mage has spent 4 editions trying to get away from. There's also the fact that the Gaia aligned factions seem to operate on a principle of theological voluntarism that is presented as the absolute, in-canon right answer. </div> </div> </div>I don't feel that the Werewolf books present the Werewolves as all knowing and completely right, but rather they are profoundly unprepared and underequipped to deal with the complexities of the situation and their attempts to simplify things only make things worse. &quot;Weaver bad&quot; except all these Gaian spirits that are technological. &quot;Wyld Good&quot; except those dangerous wyld spirits and manifestations. Now One can argue on the Middle Umbral level something is fundimentally wrong with the Weaver and wyrm they are broken on some level but that's just one part of the complex tapestry that is existence.. especially if its a mage game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, the individual Tribes and Breeds do have some compelling stuff in them. Their histories and conflicts are pretty interesting and they certainly have some neat powers and abilities to showcase when it comes time for a gonzo action scene. For better or worse, I also kinda' enjoy a lot of the Wyrm's trappings, particularly Pentex, which is such a cartoonishly nonsensical caricature it comes off as almost endearing. </div> </div> </div>Use them. This is Mage belief if power. Both in the most litteral sense and the figurative. &quot;Truth&quot; matters very little in setting, just treat the garou and company as just another Paradigm, while the Hermetic Magesplains how they are really Umbrood of this court and the whole &quot;Gaia thing&quot; is quaint, and the Akashic understands that they are manifestations of imbalance and rejection of the 8fold truths etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T13:24:16-07:00","id":1198822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves?p=1197798#post1197798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. I suppose it was a little bit pompous of me to assume that people were already familiar with my opinions. I just wanted to avoid being &quot;that guy&quot; on the forums that constantly trumpets one opinion very loudly and frequently, y'know?<br /> <br /> Basically, I think the whole shtick with the Triat is kind of problematically reductive. I <i>especially </i>don't like the way that the Weaver is said to pervade all aspects of technology and civilization, reinforcing the obnoxious &quot;science/technology = rigid conformity&quot; theme that Mage has spent 4 editions trying to get away from. There's also the fact that the Gaia aligned factions seem to operate on a principle of theological voluntarism that is presented as the absolute, in-canon right answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>All members of the Triat have stakes in the world, technology included, since there are Wyldlings of advanced medical care, scary stories told on the internet, social outrage, superheroes (who don't even know that they're really spirits, sometimes), and the concept of &quot;YOLO&quot;. There are also Weaver-spirits that are benevolent or semi-benevolent, such as spirits of mass transit or the joy of seeing a movie. Definition and routines can be alright; stringent control, however, is another part of the Weaver, and the Book of the Weaver mentioned that it was often at odds with manifestations of the Weaver that had anything to do with positives we see in life. You can make the effort to accept Downtown Bus but wrestle with the manifestations of the Patriarch; a lot of urban werewolves spend their lives doing this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> The complexities of the Weaver, however, mean that a lot of tribes just won't trust spirits in league with it, and they aren't really wrong for minimizing their associations with it when there are other spirits, particularly Gaian ones such as gridlock-beetles and crowdfunding-spirits, that can accomplish the same ends. This is particularly true if those Garou know of Drones and how they come about from exposure to the OneSong; that even makes most Glass Walkers wary of potential allies among the spinner's brood. Add on the apparent uncaring nature of werespiders (assuming that you're not dealing with a Hatar that hasn't managed to stay so impersonal), and you have a lot less certainty in trying to navigate the cosmolgy of the Triat. Their manifestations are beautiful, dangerous, and seductive, even more so for not being banes trying to honey up a potential mark.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I've also typically seen Mage as being stuck far more in problematic reduction for having technology be another form of magic. However, in this case, there's a rare instance of what's good for one being good for the other, as the dividing line of the Technocracy being Pattern because they're about control over discovery and application can also kind of work for discerning different types of Weaver-spirits, assuming that you decide to use W:tA's cosmology as-is or close to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, the individual Tribes and Breeds do have some compelling stuff in them. Their histories and conflicts are pretty interesting and they certainly have some neat powers and abilities to showcase when it comes time for a gonzo action scene. For better or worse, I also kinda' enjoy a lot of the Wyrm's trappings, particularly Pentex, which is such a cartoonishly nonsensical caricature it comes off as almost endearing. </div> </div> </div>If Pentex is cartoonish, then we're living in a world that's awfully close to Saturday morning fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T13:41:05-07:00","id":1198830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves?p=1198822#post1198822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All members of the Triat have stakes in the world, technology included, since there are Wyldlings of advanced medical care, scary stories told on the internet, social outrage, superheroes (who don't even know that they're really spirits, sometimes), and the concept of &quot;YOLO&quot;. There are also Weaver-spirits that are benevolent or semi-benevolent, such as spirits of mass transit or the joy of seeing a movie. Definition and routines can be alright; stringent control, however, is another part of the Weaver, and the Book of the Weaver mentioned that it was often at odds with manifestations of the Weaver that had anything to do with positives we see in life. You can make the effort to accept Downtown Bus but wrestle with the manifestations of the Patriarch; a lot of urban werewolves spend their lives doing this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> The complexities of the Weaver, however, mean that a lot of tribes just won't trust spirits in league with it, and they aren't really wrong for minimizing their associations with it when there are other spirits, particularly Gaian ones such as gridlock-beetles and crowdfunding-spirits, that can accomplish the same ends. This is particularly true if those Garou know of Drones and how they come about from exposure to the OneSong; that even makes most Glass Walkers wary of potential allies among the spinner's brood. Add on the apparent uncaring nature of werespiders (assuming that you're not dealing with a Hatar that hasn't managed to stay so impersonal), and you have a lot less certainty in trying to navigate the cosmolgy of the Triat. Their manifestations are beautiful, dangerous, and seductive, even more so for not being banes trying to honey up a potential mark.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I've also typically seen Mage as being stuck far more in problematic reduction for having technology be another form of magic. However, in this case, there's a rare instance of what's good for one being good for the other, as the dividing line of the Technocracy being Pattern because they're about control over discovery and application can also kind of work for discerning different types of Weaver-spirits, assuming that you decide to use W:tA's cosmology as-is or close to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I suppose you have a point there. I guess I've just been kind of put off by some of the later Revised stuff taking a more hardline &quot;Anti-Weaver&quot; stance and having the Glass Walkers Take A Level in Villainy. If there really is material that portrays technology and culture as benevolent, then I suppose I have less of a problem with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves?p=1198822#post1198822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Pentex is cartoonish, then we're living in a world that's awfully close to Saturday morning fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I get that you're trying to make a point about corporate excess in the real world, which is a <i>massive </i>problem and one of the most toxic influences on modern society, I agree. But <i>come on!</i><br /> <br /> PENTEX doesn't just try to leverage political corruption into wild deregulation in order to get away with a lower threshold on quality control, they <i>sell energy drinks that turn people into Fomori! </i><br /> <br /> I mean, c'mon. Reread Subsidiaries: A Guide To PENTEX. For every example that could plausibly be an example of real-world corporate negligence, there's a PENTEX plot to <i>use a G.I. Joe knockoff to turn children into Manchurian Candidates for the war against Gaia! </i><br /> <br /> They're not necessarily Captain Planet villains (if only because their pollution-based plots are some of their more believable and subdued projects.), but they are definitely the villains from They Live! or The Stuff. And I'm sorry, those movies are <i>ridiculous.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 03-23-2018, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T14:26:29-07:00","id":1198844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1197775-skirting-around-the-werewolves?p=1198830#post1198830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. I suppose you have a point there. I guess I've just been kind of put off by some of the later Revised stuff taking a more hardline &quot;Anti-Weaver&quot; stance and having the Glass Walkers Take A Level in Villainy. If there really is material that portrays technology and culture as benevolent, then I suppose I have less of a problem with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was not actually the Glass Walker presentation in revised. They never ended up painted as villains; they got to take down their own CyberDog problem, .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, I get that you're trying to make a point about corporate excess in the real world, which is a <i>massive </i>problem and one of the most toxic influences on modern society, I agree. But <i>come on!</i><br /> <br /> PENTEX doesn't just try to leverage political corruption into wild deregulation in order to get away with a lower threshold on quality control, they <i>sell energy drinks that turn people into Fomori! </i> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It sells a lot of products that agitate banes, which is probably not all that difficult an effect to produce. Anything guaranteed to turn humans into fomori tends to see much more selective use, such as in subverting spies working against them (hello there Mr. Iguana from Rage) or in experimental projects. Most product contamination, however, has ended up being due to lax regulatory practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, c'mon. Reread Subsidiaries: A Guide To PENTEX. For every example that could plausibly be an example of real-world corporate negligence, there's a PENTEX plot to <i>use a G.I. Joe knockoff to turn children into Manchurian Candidates for the war against Gaia! </i> </div> </div> </div>Subsidiaries was a stepping stone that still had material that clashed with the setting. Most of that didn't make it into the Revised presentation of Pentex. Sometimes, Subsidiaries also disagreed with itself; the Tellus chapter commented on how putting banes in everything was dumb on every level, but then you had the Magadon chapter of screwy stuff all over and nerve gas bypassing Resist Toxin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're not necessarily Captain Planet villains (if only because their pollution-based plots are some of their more believable and subdued projects.), but they are definitely the villains from They Live! or The Stuff. And I'm sorry, those movies are <i>ridiculous.</i> </div> </div> </div>Those movies are more Reckoning than Apocalypse. Werewolf draws way more from Upton Sinclair's <i>The Jungle</i>, particularly in how it presents meat packing in O'Tolley's as sometimes letting long pork slip through QA. That doesn't turn people into banes, but there are banes that only possess cannibals, even if they don't know they did it by accident.<br /> <br /> Another source would be the Jim Henson production Dinosaurs, in the form of the Wesayso Corporation. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WhQG54QvTTc\" target=\"_blank\">Profits are up in Q3! World ending? That's a Q4 problem.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-23-2018, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}